    <string name="smart_features_label">Smart Features</string>
    <string name="smart_keyboard_title">Smart Keyboard Detection</string>
    <string name="smart_keyboard_desc">Pause capture while you type. Detects the keyboard window, a focused text field, and recent typing, so it works even with keyboards that hide themselves from the system.</string>

    <string name="instruction_setup">To get started:\n\n1. Tap the button above\n2. Find \"DoubleTap Screenshot\" in the list\n3. Toggle it ON and confirm\n\nOnce enabled, choose a trigger below. Nothing visible is added to your screen.</string>

    <string name="instruction_active">Double-tap any corner of the screen to take a screenshot.\n\nOnly the corners respond, because a double-tap in the middle of the screen is the same gesture apps use for zoom and like.\n\nA short vibration confirms the capture, and there is a 2-second cooldown.</string>

    <string name="instruction_active_a11y">Swipe up from the bottom of the screen with two fingers to take a screenshot.\n\nChoose between the two-finger swipe and a floating button in Settings → Accessibility → DoubleTap Screenshot → Shortcut. Android recognises the gesture itself, so it never fires by accident.</string>

    <string name="instruction_paused">Detection is paused. Tap Resume to start capturing screenshots again.</string>

